{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>They pour out, etc.</b> He speaks of idol worshippers. הזלים — many have derived it from the root אזל 'to exhaust' (1 Samuel 9:7), and it is deficient alef. But the correct view is that there is no problem with it, for אזל is an intransitive verb, and its meaning is 'those who give gold from their purse.' Now in the Torah: 'stones in a bag' (Deuteronomy 25:13), and there it is with scales. Also קנה likewise — its meaning is clear and there is no problem with it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "The verse words הזלים and קנה refer to Isaiah 46:6; Ibn Ezra discusses their grammatical form and meaning without restating the full verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:18.737453432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}